                                             1. GENERAL

                        Wind shear reports that are relayed by ATC to other ACFT will contain as many of
                            the following details as possible:

                                  -  ACFT type that reported the wind shear;
                                   -  Description of event (light/moderate severe, or positive/negative);
                                  -  Height/altitude wind shear encountered;
                                  -  Phase of flight;
                                  -  RWY;
                                  -  Time of encounter;
                                   -  MET/operational information as received from the reporting pilot;
                                  -  Effect on ACFT and/or action taken by the pilot.

